   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At x = 4 the numerator is 4 - sqrt(16) = 0 and the denominator is 4 - 4 = 0, so the form is zero over zero.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate x + sqrt(x + 12). The numerator becomes x^2 - (x + 12) = x^2 - x - 12 = (x - 4)(x + 3), so the quotient is (x - 4)(x + 3)/((x - 4)(x + sqrt(x + 12))).",
         "mathjson": [
